{"schema_version":1,"source_commit":"100560de6c9f68c2875097d40a2012a84c784179","scope":"Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam Canto 2, Chapter 7 — Śrīdhara Svāmī word-for-word gloss","source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","entries":[{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":1,"end":1,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["सप्तमे","in the seventh [canto]"],["भगवल्-लीला-अवताराः","the Lord's incarnations for his pastimes"],["ब्रह्मणा उदिताः","spoken by Brahmā"],["तत्-कर्म","their acts"],["प्रयोजन-गुणैः सह","together with their purposes and qualities"],["यत्र यदा","when"],["क्षिति-तल-उद्धरण-अर्थम्","for lifting the earth"],["वाराहीं तनुं बिभ्रत्","bearing the form of a boar"],["अनन्तः उद्यतः","Ananta set forth"],["हिरण्याक्षं दंष्ट्रया ददार","he pierced Hiraṇyākṣa with his tusk"]],"note":"The source has “गुनैः” in the chapter-opening couplet; that spelling is not used as a WFW key."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":2,"end":2,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["यज्ञ-अवतारम्","the Yajña incarnation"],["रुचेः प्रजापतेः","from Ruci, the Prajāpati"],["आकूतेः सूनुः","the son of Ākūti"],["सुयज्ञो नाम जातः","was born named Su-yajña"],["दक्षिणायां स्व-भार्यायाम्","in his wife Dakṣiṇā"],["सुयमान् देवान् अजनयत्","he begot the gods called Suyāmas"],["इन्द्रः सन् आर्तिम् अहरत्","becoming Indra, he removed distress"],["देव-उत्पादनम्","the production of the gods"],["लोक-त्रय-आर्ति-हरणम्","the removal of distress from the three worlds"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":3,"end":3,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["कपिल-अवतारम्","the Kapila incarnation"],["कर्दमस्य प्रजापतेः गृहे","in the house of Kardama Prajāpati"],["देवहूत्यां जज्ञे","he was born to Devahūti"],["नवभिः स्त्रीभिः भगिनीभिः सह","along with his nine sisters"],["मात्रे आत्म-गतिं ब्रह्म-विद्याम् उक्तवान्","he taught his mother the knowledge of Brahman"],["गुण-सङ्ग-रूपं पङ्कम्","the mud in the form of attachment to the qualities"],["विधूय मुक्तिं प्राप्तवती","having washed it away, she attained liberation"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":4,"end":4,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["दत्तात्रेय-अवतारम्","the Dattātreya incarnation"],["मया अहम् एव तुभ्यं दत्तः","I myself have been given to you"],["यद् आह ततः स नाम्ना दत्तः जातः","because he said so, he was named Datta"],["स्व-भक्तेभ्यः","to his own devotees"],["योग-ऐश्वर्य-दानम्","the gift of yogic powers"],["पाद-पङ्कजयोः परागः","the pollen of his lotus feet"],["उभयीम् ऐहिकीम् आमुष्मिकाम्","both, worldly and otherworldly"],["भुक्ति-मुक्ति-रूपाम्","in the form of enjoyment and liberation"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":5,"end":5,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["कुमार-अवतारम्","the Kumāra incarnation"],["मे मया आदौ तपः तप्तम्","by me, austerity was performed at the beginning"],["स्व-तपसः","from my austerity"],["हरिः चतुःसनः अभूत्","Hari became the four Sanas"],["सनकः सनन्दनः सनातनः सनत्कुमारः","Sanaka, Sanandana, Sanātana and Sanatkumāra"],["सनात् अखण्डितात्","from the unbroken, eternal source"],["पूर्व-कल्पस्य सम्प्लवे","at the dissolution of the previous kalpa"],["विनष्टम् आत्म-तत्त्वम्","the lost knowledge of the Self"],["मुनयः आत्मनात्मनि अचक्षत","the sages directly perceived it within themselves"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":6,"end":6,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["नर-नारायण-अवतारम्","the Nara-Nārāyaṇa incarnation"],["धर्मस्य पत्न्यां दक्ष-दुहितरि","from Dharma's wife, Dakṣa's daughter"],["मूर्ति-संज्ञायाम्","named Mūrti"],["नारायणो नर इति मूर्ति-द्वयेन जातः","he was born as the two forms Nārāyaṇa and Nara"],["अनङ्गस्य पृतनाः","the armies of Kāma"],["आत्मनः स्व-प्रतिरूपाः","his own likenesses"],["नियम-अवलोपं व्रत-भङ्गम्","the breaking of his vow"],["घटितुं साधयितुम् न शेकुः","they could not bring it about"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":7,"end":7,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["काम-विजयी","the conqueror of desire"],["क्रोधोऽपि बिभेति","even anger is afraid"],["कृतिनः श्री-रुद्र-प्रमुखाः","the accomplished ones, led by Śrī Rudra"],["रोष-युक्तया दृष्ट्या","with an angry glance"],["कामं दहन्ति","they burn desire"],["रोषम् आत्मानं दहन्तम् अपि","even when anger burns itself"],["ते न दहन्ति","they do not burn it"],["यद्-अन्तरं मनः","the interior, the mind"],["अमलं निर्मलम्","stainless, pure"],["प्रविशन् अलं बिभेति","as it enters, it becomes very afraid"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":8,"end":8,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["चरित्रेण एव","by the story alone"],["मातुः सपत्न्याः","of his mother's co-wife"],["उदितानि उक्तानि वाक्यानि","the spoken words"],["पत्रिणः बाणाः","were arrows"],["तैर् विद्धः ध्रुवः","pierced by them, Dhruva"],["तपसे तपः तप्तुम्","to perform austerity"],["ध्रुव-गतिम् ध्रुव-पदम्","the fixed destination, the station of Dhruva"],["दिव्याः सप्तर्षयः स्तुवन्ति","the divine Seven Sages praise"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":9,"end":9,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["पृथु-अवतारम्","the Pṛthu incarnation"],["यदा अर्थितः","when he was requested"],["वेनं त्रात्वा","having rescued Vena"],["पुत्र इति पदं नाम लेभे","he received the name ‘son’"],["द्विजानां शाप-वाक्यम् एव वज्रम्","the words of the brāhmaṇas' curse were a thunderbolt"],["विप्लुष्टं पौरुषं भगम्","whose strength and majesty were destroyed"],["जगति जगद्-अर्थे","for the sake of the world"],["वसूनि अन्नादि-द्रव्याणि दुग्धा","he milked the wealth, such as food"]],"note":"The source prints “ऋसिभिः” for the sages. The phrase is noted here and not repeated as a corrected WFW key."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":10,"end":10,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["ऋषभ-अवतारम्","the Ṛṣabha incarnation"],["असौ हरिः नाभेः सुदेव्याः सूनुः आस","that Hari was the son of Nābhi and Sudevī"],["मेरुदेव्याः एव सुदेवी इति संज्ञा","Merudevī herself is also called Sudevī"],["जडवत् योगेन","by yoga, as if inert"],["नित्य-समाधिना","through constant samādhi"],["सम-दृक्","equal in vision"],["स्व-स्थः स्व-स्वरूपे स्थितः","established in his own nature"],["प्रशान्त-इन्द्रियः","with senses pacified"],["परितः मुक्त-सङ्गः","entirely free from attachment"]],"note":"The source heading has the damaged form “ऋसभावतारम्”; the WFW gives the conventional spelling “ऋषभ-अवतारम्” and records the source variant."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":11,"end":11,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["हयग्रीव-अवतारम्","the Hayagrīva incarnation"],["ब्रह्मणः मम सत्रे","at my sacrifice, Brahmā's"],["हयशीर्षा आस","he was Horse-headed"],["तपनीयं सुवर्णम्","refined gold"],["छन्दो-मयः वेद-मयः","consisting of metres, consisting of the Veda"],["मखाः तन्-मयाः","sacrifices consist of him"],["अखिला देवताः तद्-आत्मा","all deities are his self"],["अस्य श्वसतः","as he breathed"],["नासा-पुटात्","from the nostrils"],["उशतीः वेद-लक्षणाः वाचः बभूवुः","lovely speech in the form of the Veda arose"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":12,"end":12,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["मत्स्य-अवतारम्","the Fish incarnation"],["भाविना वैवस्वतेन मनुना दृष्टः","seen by the future Manu Vaivasvata"],["क्षोणी-मयः पृथ्वी-प्रधानः","consisting chiefly of earth"],["निखिल-जीव-निकायानाम् आश्रयः","the shelter of all groups of living beings"],["वेदस्य मार्गान्","the paths of the Vedas"],["मे मुखात् विस्रंसितान्","which had slipped from my mouth"],["आदाय","having taken"],["युगान्त-सलिले विजहार","he sported in the water at the end of the age"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":13,"end":13,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["कूर्म-अवतारम्","the Tortoise incarnation"],["क्षीर-उदधौ कच्छप-वपुः सन्","in the ocean of milk, taking the body of a tortoise"],["गोत्रम् मन्दर-गिरिम्","the mountain Mandara, the churning stick"],["पृष्ठेन धृतवान्","he supported on his back"],["अमृत-लब्धये","for obtaining nectar"],["उन्मथ्नतां सताम्","while the good beings churned"],["निद्रायाः क्षणः अवसरः","a moment of sleep, an opportunity"],["अद्रेः परिवर्तः परिभ्रमः","the mountain's turning, its revolving"],["कण्डूः घर्षण-सुखः","an itch that is pleasant through friction"]],"note":"The source prints “क्षिराब्धिम्” in this verse; the WFW gives the conventional spelling “क्षीराब्धिम्” and records that source variant."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":14,"end":14,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["श्री-नृसिंह-अवतारम्","the Śrī Narasiṃha incarnation"],["त्रैपिष्टपाः देवाः","the inhabitants of heaven"],["उरु-भयम् हन्ति","he destroys the great fear"],["करालं वक्त्रम्","a terrifying mouth"],["भ्रमन्त्यौ भ्रुकुट्यौ","the two moving eyebrows"],["दैत्येन्द्रं स्फुरन्तम्","the shining lord of the demons"],["आरात् समीपे","from nearby"],["गदया उपलक्षितम्","marked with a mace"],["नखैर् विददार","he tore him with his claws"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":15,"end":15,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["हरि-संज्ञक-अवतारम्","the incarnation named Hari"],["गज-यूथस्य पतिः","the lord of the elephant herd"],["तीर्थ-श्रवाः","he whose fame is sacred to hear"],["श्रवणेन एव मङ्गलम्","auspicious through hearing alone"],["नामधेयं यस्य","whose name is"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":16,"end":16,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["तद्-वचनं श्रुत्वा","having heard those words"],["शरण-अर्थिनम्","the one seeking shelter"],["हस्ते शुण्डायां प्रगृह्य","taking him by the trunk"],["नक्रस्य ग्राहस्य वदनम्","the crocodile's mouth"],["विनिपाट्य विदार्य","having split and torn"],["तस्मात् तद्-वदनात्","from its mouth"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":17,"end":17,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["वामन-अवतारम्","the Vāmana incarnation"],["अदितेः सुतानां द्वादश-आदित्यानाम् मध्ये","among Aditi's twelve sons, the Ādityas"],["अधियज्ञः यज्ञ-अधिष्ठाता विष्णुः","Viṣṇu, the presiding deity of sacrifice"],["अवरजः कनीयान् अपि","although the youngest"],["गुणैर् ज्यायान् ज्येष्ठः","greater by qualities, the eldest"],["इमांल्लोकान् विचक्रमे","he strode across these worlds"],["बलेः क्ष्मां वामन-रूपेण जगृहे","he took the earth from Bali in the form of Vāmana"],["याच्ञां विना","without being asked"],["धर्म-मार्गे वर्तमानः न चाल्यः","one established in dharma cannot be moved"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":18,"end":18,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["स्व-सालोक्य-आदि दास्यामि","I shall give you my own abode and the rest"],["विबुध-अधिपत्यम्","the sovereignty of the gods"],["पुरुषार्थः न भवति","is not the true human goal"],["उरुक्रमस्य पाद-शौचम्","the washing of Urukrama's feet"],["अपः सर्वतः धृतवतः","the waters held everywhere"],["शिखायाम् मूर्धनि","on the crown of the head"],["शुक्रेण वारितः शप्तः अपि","although checked and cursed by Śukra"],["प्रतिश्रुतं विना अन्यत् न चिकीर्षत्","he did not wish to do anything beyond his promise"],["तृतीय-पाद-पूरण-अर्थम्","to complete the third step"],["हरये आत्मानम् देहम् अपि अभिमेने","he offered even his body to Hari"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":19,"end":19,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["हंस-अवतारम्","the Swan incarnation"],["भृशं विवृद्धेन भावेन","with an intensely developed feeling"],["अत्युद्रिक्तया भक्त्या परितुष्टः","fully pleased by overflowing devotion"],["भक्ति-योगम्","bhakti-yoga"],["साधु यथा तथा उवाच","he explained in the proper way"],["ज्ञानं च ज्ञान-साधनम्","knowledge and the means of knowledge"],["भागवतं नाम","called the Bhāgavata"],["तत्त्वम् एव स-तत्त्वम्","the truth itself, along with its real nature"],["आत्म-तत्त्व-दीपकम्","illumining the truth of the Self"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":20,"end":20,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["तत्-तत् मन्वन्तर-अवतारम्","the incarnation of each manvantara"],["स्व-तेजः निजं प्रभावम्","his own brilliance, his power"],["चक्रं सुदर्शनम् बिभर्ति","he bears the Sudarśana disc"],["चक्रवत् अप्रतिहतम् प्रभावम्","an irresistible force like a wheel"],["मनु-वंश-पालकः सन्","being the protector of Manu's line"],["सत्य-लोकेऽपि","even in Satyaloka"],["स्व-कीर्तिं विस्तारयन्","expanding his own fame"],["राजसु दण्डं विधत्ते","he enforces punishment among kings"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":21,"end":21,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["धन्वन्तरि-अवतारम्","the Dhanvantari incarnation"],["पुरु-रुजां महा-रोगिणाम्","for those afflicted by great diseases"],["स्व-नाम्ना एव रुजः हन्ति","he destroys illnesses by his own name"],["अमृतम्","nectar"],["मरण-शून्यम् आयुः","life free from death"],["दैत्यैः प्रतिबद्धम्","obstructed by the demons"],["यज्ञे भागम् अवरुन्धे","he secures his share in the sacrifice"],["वेदम् अनुशास्ति","he teaches the Veda"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":22,"end":22,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["परशुराम-अवतारम्","the Paraśurāma incarnation"],["जगतः क्षयाय","for the destruction of the world"],["दैवेन उपभृतम् संवर्धितम्","nourished and strengthened by fate"],["ब्राह्मणेभ्यो द्रुह्यति","he acts hostilely toward brāhmaṇas"],["उज्झितः पन्थाः वेद-मार्गः","the abandoned path is the Vedic way"],["नरकार्तिं लिप्सति इव","he seems to desire the suffering of people"],["अवनेः कण्टक-तुल्यम् क्षत्रम्","the kṣatriyas, like thorns upon the earth"],["महात्मा हरिः उद्धन्ति","the great Lord Hari uproots"],["तीक्ष्ण-धारेण परशुना","with a sharp-edged axe"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":23,"end":23,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["राम-अवतारम्","the Rāma incarnation"],["अस्माकं ब्रह्म-आदीनाम् प्रसादे","by the favor of us, beginning with Brahmā"],["कलया भरतादि-रूपया सह","with his portion, in forms such as Bharata"],["कलाया ईशः","the Lord of the portion"],["दशरथस्य आज्ञायाम् तिष्ठन्","obeying Daśaratha's command"],["सीता-लक्ष्मणाभ्यां सहितः","accompanied by Sītā and Lakṣmaṇa"],["वनम् अविवेश","he entered the forest"],["यस्मिन् विरोधं कृत्वा रावणः नाशम् प्राप्तः","opposing him, Rāvaṇa met destruction"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":24,"end":24,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["यस्मै रामाय","to Rāma"],["उदधिः मार्गं ददौ","the ocean gave a path"],["सपदि शीघ्रम्","immediately, swiftly"],["हरः यथा त्रिपुरं दिधक्षुः","like Śiva desiring to burn the three cities"],["अरि-पुरं लङ्काम्","the city of the enemy, Laṅkā"],["दूरे वर्तमाना सुहृत् सीता","his beloved Sītā, far away"],["मथितः क्षुभितः रोषः","his anger stirred and agitated"],["सुशोणा दृष्टिः","his glance was intensely red"],["मकराणाम् उरगाणां नक्राणां च चक्रम्","schools of fish, serpents and crocodiles"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":25,"end":25,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["रावणस्य वक्षः-स्थल-स्पर्शेन","by contact with Rāvaṇa's chest"],["रुग्णा भग्नाः दन्ताः","the broken tusks"],["महेन्द्र-वाहस्य ऐरावतस्य","of Airāvata, Indra's mount"],["विडम्बिताः स्व-धवलिम्ना","made bright by their whiteness"],["ककुभः दिशः","the quarters, the directions"],["दार-हर्तुः रावणस्य","of Rāvaṇa, the abductor of his wife"],["महा-गर्वेण ऊढं हासम्","the great arrogance and laughter"],["असुभिः सह सद्यः विनेष्यति","he will quickly remove along with his life"],["धनुषः विस्फूर्जितैः टङ्कार-घोषैः","with the twanging sounds of his bow"],["अधि सैन्ये स्व-पर-सैन्य-मध्ये","in the midst of his own and the enemy's armies"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":26,"end":26,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["श्री-कृष्ण-अवतारम्","the Śrī Kṛṣṇa incarnation"],["सुरेतराः असुर-अंश-भूताः राजानः","the kings who were portions of demons"],["वरूथैः सैन्यैः","with armies"],["विमर्दितायाः भूमेः","of the earth, crushed under the burden"],["रामेण सह कलया जातः","born with Rāma as a portion"],["सित-कृष्णौ केशौ","the white and dark locks"],["शोभा एव न वयः-परिणाम-कृता","beauty, not a change caused by age"],["अविकारित्वात्","because of his unchanging nature"],["भू-भार-अवतरण-रूपं कार्यम्","the task of relieving the earth's burden"],["राम-कृष्णयोः वर्ण-सूचनार्थम्","to indicate the complexions of Rāma and Kṛṣṇa"],["आत्मनो महिमा","his own glory"],["उपनिबध्यते अभिव्यज्यते","is described, is manifested"]],"note":"The source debates the Purāṇic reading about Kṛṣṇa's hair and incarnation. This WFW glosses Śrīdhara's analysis and does not settle that textual question."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":27,"end":27,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["तोकेन इति","with the word ‘child’"],["बालेन पूतनायाः जीव-हरणम्","the child taking the life of Pūtanā"],["रिङ्गता जानुभ्यां गच्छता","crawling on his knees"],["अन्तरं गतेन मध्यं प्राप्तेन","having entered the midst"],["दिवि-स्पृशोः अत्युच्चयोः","of the two very tall ones reaching the sky"],["इतरथा अनीश्वरत्वे","otherwise, if he were not the Lord"],["तत् न भवितव्यम्","that could not have occurred"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":28,"end":28,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["विष-तोय-पीतान्","those who drank poisonous water"],["पालान् गोपान् च","the cowherds"],["कृपा-दृष्टि-सुधा-वृष्ट्या","with the nectar-rain of his merciful glance"],["जीवयिष्यति","he will revive"],["उरगं कालियम् उच्चाटयिष्यति","he will drive away the serpent Kāliya"],["तच्-छुद्धये","to purify that river"],["अति-विष-वीर्येण","with extremely poisonous power"],["विलोला जिह्वा यस्य","whose tongue flickers"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":29,"end":29,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["दिव्यम् अलौकिकम्","divine, otherworldly"],["उन्नेष्यति उद्धरिष्यति","he will lift up"],["शुचिः ग्रीष्मः","śuci is the summer month"],["दावाग्नेः हेतोः","because of the forest fire"],["अवसितः अन्त-कालः यस्य","whose end has been determined"],["स-बलः स-रामः","together with Bala, with Rāma"],["अनधिगम्यं दुर्ज्ञेयं वीर्यम्","whose power is difficult to fathom"],["नेत्रे पिधाप्य","having caused the eyes to be covered"]],"note":"A damaged footnote citation in the pinned source is excluded from the WFW."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":30,"end":30,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["उपबध्यते अनेन इति उपबन्धम्","that by which something is bound"],["शुल्बं दाम","a rope or cord"],["अमुष्य माता यशोदा अग्रहीत्","his mother Yaśodā took it"],["अमुष्य उदरे न माति","it did not fit around his belly"],["बन्धन-सम्मितं न भवति","it was not of sufficient length to bind"],["संवीक्ष्य दृष्ट्वा","having seen"],["प्रतिबोधिता निज-ऐश्वर्यं ज्ञापिता","reminded, made aware of her own divine power"],["तच् च कर्म दिव्यम् इव","that act too seemed divine"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":31,"end":31,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["वरुणस्य पाशात्","from Varuṇa's noose"],["तस्मात् भयात् मोचयिष्यति","he will free him from that fear"],["मय-सूनुना व्योम-नाम्ना","by the son of Maya, named Vyoma"],["अह्नि आपृतम् व्यापार-युक्तम्","engaged in activity during the day"],["निशि शयानम्","sleeping at night"],["उपनेष्यति प्रापयिष्यति","he will bring"],["गोकुल-वासिनं जनम्","the people of Gokula"],["स्म इत्य् आश्चर्ये","the particle sma conveys wonder"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":32,"end":32,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["देवे इन्द्रे","the god Indra"],["पशून् रिरक्षुः","desiring to protect the animals"],["अनघे श्रम-रहिते","without fatigue"],["एकस्मिन्न् एव करे","with just one hand"],["सलीलं यथा तथा","playfully, with ease"],["महीध्रं गोवर्धनम्","Govardhana, the great mountain"],["धर्ता धारयिष्यति","he will hold"],["उच्छिलीन्ध्रम् उद्गतं छत्राकम् इव","like a mushroom rising up"],["सप्त-वर्षाणि वयः यस्य","whose age was seven years"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":33,"end":33,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["निशि रात्रौ","at night"],["निशाकर-रश्मिभिः","by the moon's rays"],["गौर्यां धवलायाम्","on the pale, white ground"],["कलानि मञ्जुलानि पदानि","graceful, charming steps"],["आयतं दीर्घम् आलाप-विशेष-युक्तम्","long, extended, marked by distinctive melody"],["उद्दीपितः स्मरः","Kāma was inflamed"],["शङ्खचूडस्य शिरः हरिष्यति","he will take the head of Śaṅkhacūḍa"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":34,"end":35,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["प्रलम्बादयः","Pralamba and the others"],["ते सर्वे हरिणा हेतु-भूतेन","all those, through Hari as the cause"],["तदीयं निलयं अदर्शनम्","their unseen abode"],["वैकुण्ठम् अलं यास्यन्ति","they will surely go to Vaikuṇṭha"],["खरः धेनुकः","Khara means Dhenuka"],["दर्दुरः बकः","Dardura means Baka"],["इभः कुवलयापीडः","Ibha means Kuvalayāpīḍa"],["कुजः नरकः","Kuja means Naraka"],["कपिः द्विविदः","the monkey means Dvivida"],["समिति-शालिनः","those who boast in battle"],["व्याज-आह्वयाः कपट-नामानि","assumed names, deceptive titles"],["सप्त-उक्षाणः तेन दमिताः","the seven bulls were subdued by him"]],"note":"The source groups the commentary on 2.7.34–35; the WFW range preserves it."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":36,"end":36,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["व्यास-अवतारम्","the Vyāsa incarnation"],["अनु-युगम्","in each age"],["मीलिता संकुचिता धीर् येषाम्","whose intelligence had contracted"],["स्तोकम् अल्पम् आयुः","whose lives were short"],["स्व-निगमः स्व-कृतः वेद-राशिः","his own Veda collection, composed by himself"],["दूरे पारं यस्य","whose far shore is difficult to reach"],["सत्यवत्याम् आविर्भूतः","appearing in Satyavatī"],["विटपशः शाखा-भेदेन","as the divisions into branches"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":37,"end":37,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["बुद्ध-अवतारम्","the Buddha incarnation"],["देव-द्विषाम्","of those hostile to the gods"],["निगम-वर्त्मनि वेद-मार्गे निष्ठितानाम्","who were firmly established on the Vedic path"],["पूर्भिः पुरीभिः","by the cities"],["अदृश्य-तूर्भिः अलक्ष्य-वेगाभिः","with unseen, irresistible force"],["मतेः विमोहः योग्यता-त्यागः","confusion of judgment means abandoning discrimination"],["प्रलोभः अयुक्त-स्वीकारः","delusion means accepting the improper"],["औपधर्म्यं पाषण्ड-धर्मम्","the counterfeit dharma of heretics"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":38,"end":38,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["यर्हि यदा","when"],["सताम् अपि आलयेषु गृहेषु","even in the homes of the virtuous"],["हरेः कथा न स्युः","there are no narrations of Hari"],["त्रैवर्णिकाः पाषण्डिनः","the three higher classes become heretical"],["शूद्राः राजानः","śūdras become kings"],["कलेः शास्ता भविष्यति","he will become the chastiser of Kali"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":39,"end":39,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["सृष्ट्य्-आदि-कार्य-भेदेन","according to the differences among acts beginning with creation"],["माया-गुण-अवतार-विभूतीः","the manifestations of the incarnations of māyā's qualities"],["सर्गः","creation"],["स्थाने स्थितौ","maintenance means remaining in place"],["मखः विष्णुः","sacrifice means Viṣṇu"],["धर्मः मखः मनवः अमराः अवनीशाः","dharma, sacrifice, Manus, gods and kings"],["अन्ते संहारे","at the end, in dissolution"],["हरः रुद्रः","Hara means Rudra"],["मन्यु-वशाः सर्पाः","those under anger's sway are serpents"],["बहु-शक्ति-धारिणः","possessing many powers"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":40,"end":40,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["पृथिव्याः परमाणून्","the atoms of the earth"],["विममे गणितवान्","measured, counted"],["विष्णोः वीर्य-गणनाम्","the power of Viṣṇu"],["कर्तुम् अर्हति","who could undertake?"],["त्रि-पृष्ठं सत्य-लोकम्","the upper worlds and Satyaloka"],["चस्कम्भ धृतवान्","he supported"],["त्रैविक्रमे","in the three strides"],["स्व-रंहसा स्व-पाद-वेगेन","by his own swift stride"],["त्रि-साम्य-रूपं सदनम्","the abode characterized by the equilibrium of the three qualities"],["सर्वं धृतवान्","he supported everything"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":41,"end":41,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["पुरुषस्य माया-बलम्","the power of the Person's māyā"],["अन्तं न विदामि","I do not know the limit"],["दश-शतानि आननानि यस्य","he of a thousand faces"],["शेषः अपि","even Śeṣa"],["अस्य गुणान् गायन्","singing his qualities"],["पारं न समवस्यति","does not reach the end"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":42,"end":42,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["दयया दयां कुर्यात्","if he shows compassion"],["निर्व्यलीकम् निष्कपटम्","without deceit, sincerely"],["आश्रित-चरणः","taking shelter at his feet"],["दुस्तरां देव-मायाम् अतितरन्ति","they cross the difficult divine māyā"],["माया-वैभवं विदन्ति","they also know māyā's power"],["श्व-शृगालानां भक्ष्ये देहे","in the body, food for dogs and jackals"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":43,"end":45,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["अन्तर्-ज्ञान-अभावेऽपि","even without inward knowledge"],["मायेयम् इति ज्ञानम्","the understanding ‘this is māyā’"],["तत्-कृपया बहूनाम् अस्ति","exists for many by his grace"],["यूयम् इति","the word ‘you’"],["सनक-आदीन् अन्तर्भाव्य","including Sanaka and the others"],["दैत्य-वर्यः प्रह्लादः","the foremost of demons, Prahlāda"],["मनुः स्वायम्भुवः","Svāyambhuva Manu"],["तस्य पत्नी शतरूपा","his wife Śatarūpā"],["तद्-आत्मजाः प्रियव्रत-उत्तानपादौ","his sons Priyavrata and Uttānapāda"],["अङ्गः वेन-पिता","Aṅga, the father of Vena"],["उपेन्द्रदत्तः शुकः","Śuka, given by Upendra"],["विभीषणादयः वर्याः मुख्या येषाम्","Vibhīṣaṇa and other principal leaders"]],"note":"The Śrīdhara source groups 2.7.43–45 in one commentary block; the WFW range preserves it."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":46,"end":46,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["सत्-सङ्गेन","through the association of the good"],["अद्भुताः क्रमाः पाद-न्यासाः","wonderful strides, the steps of his feet"],["तत्-परायणाः तद्-भक्ताः","devoted to him, his devotees"],["शीले शिक्षा येषाम्","whose conduct is a lesson"],["ते अपि विदन्ति","they too know"],["श्रुत-धारणा ब्राह्मणाः","the learned, who retain what they hear"],["देव-मायाम् विदन्ति","they know the Lord's māyā"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":47,"end":48,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["भगवतः स्वरूपम्","the nature of Bhagavān"],["यद् ब्रह्म इति विदुः मुनयः","that which sages know as Brahman"],["अजस्रं नित्यम्","uninterrupted, eternal"],["सुखं विशोकं च","blissful and free from sorrow"],["शश्वत् सदा प्रशान्तम्","always and forever peaceful"],["अभयम्","fearless"],["समं भेद-शून्यम्","even, without distinction"],["प्रतिबोध-मात्रं ज्ञान-एक-रसम्","pure awareness, consisting solely of knowledge"],["शुद्धं निर्मलम्","pure, stainless"],["सद्-असतः परम्","beyond the existent and nonexistent"],["आत्म-तत्त्वम् आत्मनो ज्ञातुः स्वरूपम्","the truth of the Self, the nature of the knower"],["यत्र क्रिया-फलम् नास्ति","where no product of action exists"],["आनन्द-अंश-अभिव्यक्तिः","only the manifestation of a portion of bliss"],["माया-अभिमुखे स्थातुं विलज्जमानेव","as if māyā is ashamed to stand before him"],["सध्र्यङ् सहचरम्","sadhryaṅ means a companion"],["नियम्य यस्मिन् स्थिरीकृत्य","having restrained and fixed [the mind] in him"],["यतयः कृतार्थाः","the ascetics, whose purpose is fulfilled"],["न किम् अपि कृत्यम् अस्ति","have no further duty"],["साधनं जह्युः त्यजेयुः","they should abandon the means"],["अनुपयोगात् न आद्रियन्ते","they do not value it because it is no longer useful"]],"note":"The pinned source groups 2.7.47–48. A noisy foreign-language editorial note in the source footnote is excluded from the WFW."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":49,"end":49,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["अजस्र-सुखं विशोकं ब्रह्म","Brahman, unceasing bliss and free from sorrow"],["भगवतः स्वरूपम्","the nature of Bhagavān"],["प्राक्","before that attainment"],["स एव सर्व-फल-दाता","he alone gives all results"],["सर्व-कर्म-प्रवर्तकः","the initiator of all actions"],["स्वर्ग-आदीनां दाता","the giver of heaven and the rest"],["स्वारम्भक-धातूनाम्","of the elements from which the body began"],["अन्व् अनु विशीर्यमाणे देहे","while the body is gradually breaking apart"],["व्योम् न विशीर्यते","space does not fall apart"],["अजः तेन सह न जातः","the unborn Self was not born with it"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":50,"end":50,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["अध्याय-त्रयस्य अर्थम्","the meaning of the three chapters"],["स एष संक्षेपेण अभिहितः","this has been explained in brief"],["सद्-असत् कार्यं कारणं च","the existent and nonexistent, effect and cause"],["हरेर् अन्यत् न भवति","is not separate from Hari"],["विकार-प्रसङ्गः","the possibility of modification"],["कारण-भूतः हरिः","Hari, who is the cause"],["कार्याद् व्यतिरिक्तः","distinct from the effect"]],"note":"The source joins words in “सोऽयं तेसमासेन” and “हरेरन्यन्”; the WFW separates them as “स एष संक्षेपेण” and “हरेर् अन्यत्” and records the spacing repair."},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":51,"end":51,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["विभूतीनाम् संग्रहः","a collection of manifestations"],["उदितः","has been stated"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":52,"end":52,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["यथा वर्णितेन","in the manner described"],["नृणां भक्तिः भविष्यति","devotion will arise in people"],["इति संकल्प्य संचिन्त्य","having resolved, having reflected"],["हरि-लीला-प्राधान्येन","with the pastimes of Hari as the main subject"],["श्रीमद्-भागवतम् वर्णय","describe the Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam"],["भक्ति-रस-विघातेन","by obstructing the taste of devotion"],["केवलं तत्त्वम् न","not merely abstract doctrine"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":7,"start":53,"end":53,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/07_avatAra-sanxepaH.md","source_blob_sha":"a4e1624a10fc588b6384c7031b2221865f4249ce","pairs":[["लीला मायाश्रया","the pastimes depend on māyā"],["किं तद्-वर्णनेन","what is the use of describing them?"],["मायाम् इति","with the word ‘māyā’"]]}]}